Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• year / month / day / hour: build the calendar day that each observation belongs to and to constrain the 2005‑2015 time‑span.  
• latitude / longitude: returned coordinates for the highest‑wind days.  
• wind_speed: the element to be averaged; records are stored in tenths of a m s‑¹, so NULL or NaN must be excluded.  
• timestamp (already UTC): can be a convenient alternative instead of the year / month / day triplet.  
Typical filter conditions  
• year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015  
• wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT NaN  
• In some drafts we may also want to keep only positive wind speeds (wind_speed > 0).

────────────────────────────────────────
Ten exploratory → analytical queries
Each returns ≤ 20 rows and illustrates a different step, ending with the required answer; all are written for the public project `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads`.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at a single table (2008) to understand the basic columns.
SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2008`
WHERE  wind_speed IS NOT NULL
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List every distinct reporting year that exists inside the 2005‑2015 tables.
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM (
  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2005`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2006`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2007`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2008`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2009`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2011`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2012`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2013`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2014`
  UNION ALL  SELECT year FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2015`
)
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Retrieve some non‑missing wind observations in the whole period.
SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
FROM (
  SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2009`
  UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
)
WHERE year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015
  AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect how large wind values look (ordered sample).
SELECT year, month, day, hour, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
WHERE  wind_speed IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY wind_speed DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Daily‑average wind at one grid‑point for one table.
SELECT
  year, month, day,
  AVG(wind_speed) AS avg_daily_wind_tenths_ms
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2007`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY year, month, day
ORDER BY avg_daily_wind_tenths_ms DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Build a DATE column once (on 2008 only) to show the idea.
SELECT
  DATE(year, month, day) AS obs_date,
  latitude,
  longitude,
  wind_speed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2008`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Combine three consecutive tables and compute the ten largest daily means.
WITH unioned AS (
  SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2008`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2009`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
)
SELECT
  DATE(year, month, day) AS obs_date,
  AVG(wind_speed)        AS avg_daily_wind
FROM unioned
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY obs_date
ORDER BY avg_daily_wind DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as #7 but keep one representative lat/lon per day (centroid of records).
WITH unioned AS (
  SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2008`
  UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2009`
  UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
)
SELECT
  DATE(year, month, day)                AS obs_date,
  AVG(wind_speed)                       AS avg_daily_wind,
  AVG(latitude)   AS approx_latitude,
  AVG(longitude)  AS approx_longitude
FROM unioned
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY obs_date
ORDER BY avg_daily_wind DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

